FQN: Example: Probe a PNG stream asynchronously
Kind: verified_example
Provenance: authored
Verification: passed
Authored example: written for foss-mcp against the pinned library, not taken from the upstream README; published only after the ingestion verifier compiled or ran it against that commit.
Wraps a minimal PNG header in a MemoryStream and awaits ImageProbe.ProbeAsync with top-level await, then prints the format and size it reports.

Example:
// Authored example: probe a stream asynchronously with ProbeAsync
using System;
using System.IO;
using System.Threading;
using System.Threading.Tasks;
using Aspose.Imaging.Foss;

byte[] png =
{
    // PNG signature.
    0x89, 0x50, 0x4E, 0x47, 0x0D, 0x0A, 0x1A, 0x0A,
    // IHDR chunk: length (13), type, width (2), height (3), bit depth (8), color type (6).
    0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x0D, 0x49, 0x48, 0x44, 0x52,
    0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x02, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x03, 0x08, 0x06,
};

using var stream = new MemoryStream(png);
ImageInfo info = await ImageProbe.ProbeAsync(stream, CancellationToken.None);
Console.WriteLine($"{info.Format}: {info.Width}x{info.Height}, {info.BitDepth}-bit");
Source-Commit: c5e77bdc7b4a5c19190b6dfae5ae9d420b5886fa

